# What never goes into the data server's image. A pattern without **/ matches at the top of the folder only; **/ matches in every folder.
# This computer's own runtimes and caches, secrets, the history, leftovers:
.git
.github
.venv
runtime
.cache
.secrets
.userdata
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
_netrc
*.secret
scripts/_cache
node_modules
_site
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.part
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
*.command
*.bat
PRESENTATION.md
MOVING.md

# The website: Azure Static Web Apps serves it with its own security headers, so the data server's name never hands out a second copy of the pages.
# A request for a page there finds nothing (404); every /api address answers as before.
index.html
design.html
manifest.json
robots.txt
favicon.ico
sw.js
js
css
vendor
icons
design
docs
deploy

# scripts/push.mjs stays in: the reminder pushes need one copy always awake (min and max replicas 1) and a lasting disk (the Azure Files share mounted at
# /var/cache/crophalo), which the container app has. With min replicas 0 or no share the push keys and the browsers' subscriptions would be lost.

# The checks and their recorded answers run on GitHub and on the owners' computers, not on the server.
scripts/fixtures
scripts/vendor-test
scripts/test_*.mjs
scripts/e2e*.mjs
scripts/live_check_*.mjs
scripts/record_*.mjs
